From: Julien Etienne <julien.etienne@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 05:42:32 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 390/394] dt-bindings: power: mediatek: mt6797-scpsys: describe
 the CONN power controller

The MT6797 SCPSYS node also carries a power-controller child that
registers the CONN domain, which the connectivity subsystem owner
attaches to without powering it. Allow the simple-mfd compatible, the
child node and the address cells it needs.

Part of the clean MT6797 Wi-Fi series (Wi-Fi daily-use plan, phase 1).
The content is the station series' CONN-domain binding, unchanged.
---
 .../bindings/power/mediatek,mt6797-scpsys.yaml        | 11 +++++++++++
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+)

diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/power/mediatek,mt6797-scpsys.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/power/mediatek,mt6797-scpsys.yaml
index fc1e99df3..6696af5bf 100644
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/power/mediatek,mt6797-scpsys.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/power/mediatek,mt6797-scpsys.yaml
@@ -24,6 +24,8 @@ properties:
     items:
       - const: mediatek,mt6797-scpsys
       - const: syscon
+      - const: simple-mfd
+    minItems: 2
 
   reg:
     maxItems: 1
@@ -35,6 +37,15 @@ properties:
   '#power-domain-cells':
     const: 1
 
+  '#address-cells':
+    const: 1
+
+  '#size-cells':
+    const: 0
+
+  power-controller:
+    $ref: /schemas/power/mediatek,power-controller.yaml#
+
   clocks:
     minItems: 4
     maxItems: 4
